A recommended approach is to wrap your fetch calls within a `createServerFn`, which allows you to access the server context.
Here’s how you can set this up: instead of placing your fetch directly in the route loader, encapsulate it within a Server Function.
This ensures that the code runs exclusively on the server and provides access to the incoming web request.
