If you are making modifications to data (like POST, PUT, or DELETE) and your ASP.NET backend requires an Anti-Forgery / CSRF token in addition to the cookie, you'll need to extract that token from the `getWebRequest()` headers as well and include it in your fetch request, just as you did with the cookie.

